    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§206 & 4310, Pub Health L; amd §6, Chap of 2024 (as proposed in S.8456 & A.7079)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S814\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to organ donation\nregistration through a patient-facing portal; and to amend a chapter of\nthe laws of 2024 amending the public health law relating to allowing\npatients to register in the \"donate life registry\" through their elec-\ntronic health records, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.  8456\nand A. 7079, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2023,\nc.662, to allow a patient to register in the Donate Life Registry\nthrough their electronic health records\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by requiring the regis-\ntration to the Donate Life America (DLA) registry be through a patient-\nfacing portal of the electronic health record (EHR). The chapter also\nrequires that EHR products do not retain or store patient information to\nprotect patient confidentiality and prevent conflicts of interest that\ncan arise if the facility is aware of the patient's donor status prior\nto the point the patient meets criteria for determination of suitability\nfor organ donation.\n\nThis legislation also amends the underlying chapter by requiring the EHR\nproducts to meet standards set by the Department of Health, including\nbut not limited to using a standardized question that allows direct\nenrollment in the Donate Life registry and required data elements.\n\nLastly, this legislation amends the underlying chapter by extending the\neffective date to two years from enactment to provide more compliance\ntime for hospitals and vendors. The chapter also requires that any\nregistrations within 2 years of enactment be transmitted to the Donate\nLife New York State (DLNYS) registry in addition to DLA.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 662 of the Laws of 2024. S.8456 and A.7079\npassed the Senate and Assembly in March and May 2024, respectively.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided that sections one, two\nand three of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the public health law\nrelating to allowing patients to register in the \"donate life registry\"\nthrough their electronic health records, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S. 8456 and A. 7079, takes effect.\n",
